{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`enrich_drain._spawn_detached_drain` starts the detached drain child with\n`subprocess.Popen([...], env=..., stdin=..., stdout=..., stderr=log_fh, **_detach_kwargs())` —\nwith **no `cwd=`**. The child therefore inherits the parent's working directory.\n\nrebar's own workflow creates short-lived worktrees and removes them (`make worktree` /\n`git worktree remove`). When a write from inside such a worktree spawns a drain child and the\nworktree is later removed, the child's inherited cwd no longer exists. `queue.claim` calls\n`_tracker(repo_root)` -> `config.tracker_dir` -> `_config_sources.repo_root` -> `Path.cwd()`,\nand `os.getcwd()` raises:\n\n```\nFileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory\n```\n\nThe drain aborts before claiming anything.\n\n## Evidence (2026-08-20, this repo's own store)\n\n`.rebar/logs/enrich-drain.log` carries this traceback for **four distinct removed worktrees**:\n\n```\n/Users/joeoakhart/rebar-ci-latency-debug\n/Users/joeoakhart/rebar-debug-structured-duplicates\n/Users/joeoakhart/rebar-debug-zizmor-online\n/Users/joeoakhart/split-config-writer\n```\n\nThe store currently holds **3 permanently pending enrichment entries** that never drain:\n\n```\n8625-7bea-67db-4cdc   9305-b42c-3262-4c58   e27c-5a20-cd13-43b2\n```\n\nNotably these are also the three largest ticket directories in the store (870 / 747 / 621\nevent files) — the most re-certified tickets, so the ones most often re-enqueued.\n\n## Why this matters beyond a failed drain\n\nIt defeats the fix for `moist-short-lionfish` (958e-f4b3-275c-4154). That bug makes the\nwrite-path drain gate O(1) via a marker recording \"nothing can be pending before T\". The fast\npath is only reachable when the queue is genuinely quiet — correctly so, since a marker must\nnever be able to hide real work. With entries wedged pending forever, the gate keeps doing the\nfull O(ticket-count) store walk on every write and the 20 ms budget warning keeps firing, even\nwith 958e landed. So 958e's acceptance criterion \"the WARNING no longer fires on an ordinary\nwrite\" is not observable on this store until this is fixed.\n\n## Approach (to be confirmed by whoever claims this)\n\nPass an explicit, known-good `cwd` to the detached child rather than inheriting one that may be\ngone — the tracker's parent (the repo root) is already computed by `_rebar_dir(tracker)` and is\nthe natural choice. Consider also whether `_config_sources.repo_root`'s `Path.cwd()` fallback\nshould degrade rather than raise, since any detached/daemonised caller has the same exposure.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py` (`_spawn_detached_drain`)\n- possibly `src/rebar/_config_sources.py` (`repo_root`'s cwd fallback)\n- tests under `tests/unit/`\n\n## Testing\n- A test that spawns the drain child from a directory that is removed before the child resolves\n  the tracker, and asserts the drain still claims and processes the entry.\n- A test pinning that the child is launched with an explicit `cwd` that does not depend on the\n  caller's.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A detached drain child started from a since-removed worktree still resolves the tracker\n      and drains.\n- [x] The three wedged entries above drain (or an equivalent reproduction does).\n- [x] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and CI's pytest invocation are green.\n\n## Provenance\nFound while debugging 958e-f4b3-275c-4154 (moist-short-lionfish) — the reason that bug's fix\ncannot be observed end-to-end on this store. Out of that ticket's scope (different file,\ndifferent mechanism), filed rather than folded in."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787271539013359001,"uuid":"a227917e-1c29-4568-b540-862e23af231d"}